# MiniAI working rules (apply to every task)
- If your own tooling surfaces a clarifying question, STOP and report it
  back for an answer - do not pick a default and continue.
- Never commit unless the task explicitly says to commit.
- In every report, paste the FULL contents of every new file and the FULL
  diff of every changed code file. Never summarize, abbreviate or elide
  code or test output with '...' or 'see workspace'.
- Verify results independently (on disk, in the database, in logs) rather
  than trusting a model's or a script's own claims.
- Never print, log or paste secrets from .env.
- Append a dated PROJECT_LOG.md entry for every completed task.
- If full code or output is too long for the report, write ALL of it to
  logs/review_<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>_<task>.log (git-ignored) and say so at the
  top of the report. The user attaches that file. Never point to 'tool
  output above' or 'the workspace' - the reviewer cannot see either.
